8.text:
The first probe's phenol enables efficient photosensitized phenoxyl-radical formation (via the thioxanthenone under 417 nm light), yielding strong light-dependent protein labeling and Cy5 signal. Replacing it with a benzyl alcohol removes that dominant pathway, so the much weaker residual light-dependent difference must arise from the only other photoactive species still present—the thioxanthenone sensitizer itself (direct H-atom abstraction, energy/electron transfer, or background crosslinking). This matches the observed substituent dependence exactly.

B is unavailable without the phenolic OH, C would operate equally in both probes (yet the signal drops sharply), and D/E are chemically implausible or added post-irradiation. Thus the answer remains A.

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

