10.text:
The second probe lacks the phenolic OH needed for efficient phenoxyl-radical generation, abolishing the dominant labeling route and sharply attenuating the light-dependent Cy5 difference. The residual (weak but still observable) irradiation-dependent signal can therefore arise only from the sole remaining 417 nm-absorbing species capable of low-level protein modification (background HAT, energy/electron transfer, or nonspecific photo-crosslinking): the thioxanthenone sensitizer itself.  

B is chemically unavailable at useful efficiency without the free phenol. C would operate thermally and appear equally in dark controls. D/E are implausible or added post-irradiation. This matches the observed substituent dependence, wavelength dependence, and intensity collapse exactly.  

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

15.text:
The second probe replaces the phenolic OH with a hydroxymethyl group, eliminating efficient phenoxyl-radical formation (B). The residual light-dependent Cy5 difference is therefore produced by the sole remaining 417 nm-absorbing photoactive species capable of low-level protein modification: the thioxanthenone sensitizer itself (A, via background HAT/energy transfer or nonspecific photo-crosslinking). B is chemically unavailable at useful efficiency without the phenolic OH. C would be a non-light-dependent Michael acceptor unrelated to the observed irradiation and substituent dependence. D and E are chemically implausible or added after irradiation.

Thus the molecule responsible for the fluorescent difference observed with the second probe is A.

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

